<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Âu Việt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Au Viet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Âu Việt were an ancient people of the northern uplands of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. According to Vietnamese tradition, their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-duong-vuong">Thục Phán</a> overthrew the last Hùng king of Văn Lang around 258 BCE and united the Âu Việt and Lạc Việt in the kingdom of Âu Lạc.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/au-viet.jpg" alt="Âu Việt" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DannamEmpire · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Territorial_divisions_of_V%C4%83n_Lang_during_the_H%E1%BB%93ng_B%C3%A0ng_dynasty.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
